  [type] E0096

  × declared throws is `Boom`, but this function may also throw `unknown`
  │ help: declare a specific error type where `unknown` comes from: a function type or interface method written `throws unknown` should name the error type its implementations must throw
  │ help: if the `unknown` comes from code you don't control, convert it where it enters: `catch_all (e) { _ => throw baml.errors.UnknownError.from<Boom>(e) }`, then declare `throws Boom |
  │ baml.errors.UnknownError`. Removing the clause, or writing `throws Boom | _`, also compiles, but passes `unknown` on to callers
